
{% macro head(kick, title, n) -%}
<div class="kicker">{{kick}}</div><div class="hrule"></div><img class="qmark" src="{{qmark}}">
<div class="title">{{title}}</div><div class="sub">{{S.name}}&nbsp; / &nbsp;{{S.rec.locality}}</div>
<div class="foot"><b>{{'%02d' % n}}</b><span>{{S.report_id}} &nbsp;/&nbsp; {{DATE}} &nbsp;/&nbsp; {{REV}}</span></div>
{%- endmacro %}
{% set pa = sens.protected %}

<!-- 01 COVER -->
<section class="page">
  <img src="{{logo}}" style="position:absolute;left:18mm;top:20mm;width:69mm">
  <div style="position:absolute;right:18.5mm;top:57mm;text-align:right;font-style:italic;font-size:12pt;line-height:1.45">Better study,<br>better decisions.</div>
  <img src="{{layers_cover}}" style="position:absolute;left:135.7mm;top:77.5mm;width:74.3mm">
  <div style="position:absolute;left:17mm;top:84mm;font-size:39pt;font-weight:700;line-height:1.12;letter-spacing:-.8pt">Bannerughatta<br>Site<br>Report</div>
  <div style="position:absolute;left:17.6mm;top:142mm;font-size:12.5pt;color:#333">Site 1 &nbsp;·&nbsp; Sy. 21 &amp; 22 &nbsp;·&nbsp; {{fmt(geo.area_acre,2)}} acres</div>
  <div class="glbl" style="position:absolute;left:17.6mm;top:201mm;font-size:7pt">Site analysis</div>
  <div style="position:absolute;left:17.6mm;top:211mm;font-size:12pt;line-height:1.5">Prepared for Qnit case-study portfolio<br>Presented by GeoAce Studio Pvt Ltd</div>
  <div style="position:absolute;left:17.6mm;top:233.5mm;font-size:8pt;color:#666;line-height:1.55">Bannerughatta, Anekal taluk, Bengaluru Urban &nbsp;·&nbsp; {{geo.centroid[0]}}° N, {{geo.centroid[1]}}° E<br>{{DATE}} &nbsp;/&nbsp; {{REV}} &nbsp;/&nbsp; {{S.report_id}}</div>
  <img src="{{geoace}}" style="position:absolute;left:17.6mm;top:264mm;width:47mm">
</section>

<!-- 02 OVERVIEW -->
<section class="page">{{ head('SITE OVERVIEW','The site at a glance',2) }}
 <div class="body">
  <div class="row" style="gap:5.6mm">
   <div style="width:135.5mm"><img class="fig" src="{{fig.hero}}" style="height:81mm"></div>
   <div class="col" style="padding-top:.6mm">
     <div class="lbl">Latitude</div><div class="mid" style="font-size:13pt">{{'%.6f' % geo.centroid[0]}}° N</div>
     <div class="lbl" style="margin-top:6mm">Longitude</div><div class="mid" style="font-size:13pt">{{'%.6f' % geo.centroid[1]}}° E</div>
     <div class="lbl" style="margin-top:6mm">Study extent</div><div class="mid" style="font-size:16pt">{{fmt(geo.study_extent_m)}} m</div>
     <div class="small" style="margin-top:4mm">North up · scale bar on image<br>Imagery Wayback 24 Sep 2026</div>
   </div>
  </div>
  <div class="cap"><b>SOURCE</b> &nbsp;/&nbsp; Esri World Imagery (Wayback 2026-09-24). Boundary from Case_Studies.kml, Site 1; vertices V1–V{{geo.n_edges}}, centroid in WGS 84.</div>
  <div class="row" style="margin-top:9mm;gap:0">
   <div style="width:72mm"><div class="lbl">Site area</div><div class="big">{{fmt(geo.area_m2)}} m²</div><div class="small">{{fmt(geo.area_acre,2)}} acres · {{fmt(geo.area_ha,2)}} ha · {{fmt(geo.area_guntas)}} guntas</div></div>
   <div style="width:56mm"><div class="lbl">Perimeter</div><div class="big">{{fmt(geo.perimeter_m)}} m</div><div class="small">KML boundary, Oct 2026</div></div>
   <div class="col"><div class="lbl">Boundary</div><div class="big">{{geo.n_edges}} edges</div><div class="small">Irregular polygon, about {{geo.rect_dims_m[0]}} × {{geo.rect_dims_m[1]}} m</div></div>
  </div>
  <h2 style="margin-top:8mm">Design brief</h2>
  <p style="font-size:11.6pt;line-height:1.33">A {{fmt(geo.area_ha,2)}} ha vacant, sloping parcel off Bannerghatta Road, {{fmt(pa.dist_m)}} m from Bannerghatta National Park. What can it carry under agricultural zoning and the park's eco-sensitive rules, and where do the slope, the park edge and the pending mutation set the limit?</p>
  <div class="row" style="margin-top:6mm">
   <div class="col"><div style="font-size:12pt;font-weight:700;margin-bottom:2.5mm">Primary opportunity</div><p class="grey" style="font-size:8.8pt">A park-edge setting {{fmt(R.context.major_roads.primary.dist_m)}} m from SH-87, with a bus stop at {{fmt(inf.bus_stop.dist_m)}} m and four schools within a 10-min walk. That suits a low-density, landscape-led use: institutional, nature education or farm-house living.</p></div>
   <div class="col"><div style="font-size:12pt;font-weight:700;margin-bottom:2.5mm">Key constraint</div><p class="grey" style="font-size:8.8pt">{{zone_top[1]}}% Agriculture on the draft RMP 2031 layer. The park boundary lies {{fmt(pa.dist_m)}} m {{pa.bearing}}, so the eco-sensitive zone (100 m–1 km, under Supreme Court review) may apply. Sy 22 also has a disputed mutation pending.</p></div>
  </div>
  <div style="border-top:.6pt solid #d4d4d4;margin-top:6mm;padding-top:4.2mm;display:flex">
   <div class="glbl" style="width:56mm;font-size:7.4pt;padding-top:1mm">Report route</div>
   <div class="small" style="font-size:7.6pt">03–04 &nbsp;Site &amp; ground &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; 05–08 &nbsp;Environment<br>09–11 &nbsp;Context &amp; services &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; 12 &nbsp;Priorities &amp; sources</div>
  </div>
  <div class="small" style="margin-top:4.5mm">Stakeholders: Qnit case-study portfolio &nbsp;/&nbsp; GeoAce Studio design team &nbsp;/&nbsp; Reviewer: pending</div>
 </div>
</section>

<!-- 03 SITE DETAILS -->
<section class="page">{{ head('SITE DETAILS','Boundary, edges & development',3) }}
 <div class="body">
  <div class="row" style="gap:3mm">
   <img class="fig" src="{{fig.boundary}}" style="width:101mm;height:75mm">
   <img class="fig" src="{{fig.zoning_screenshot}}" style="width:71mm;height:75mm;object-position:40% 50%">
  </div>
  <div class="cap"><b>SOURCE</b> &nbsp;/&nbsp; Left: Esri imagery 2026; dashed = draft RMP 2031 plan roads (Qnit planning layer). Right: Qnit 2031 plan layer, BDA RMP 2031 (draft) on satellite, supplied screenshot.</div>
  <div class="row" style="margin-top:6.5mm;gap:13mm">
   <div class="col"><h2>Site identity</h2><div class="kv">
     <div>Survey / parcel &nbsp;<b>Sy. 22/*/1 (in) · 21/*/* (63 m out)</b></div>
     <div>Village / authority &nbsp;<b>Bannerughatta (613132) · BDA</b></div>
     <div>CRS / boundary &nbsp;<b>WGS 84 KML · UTM 43N</b></div>
     <div>Records / status &nbsp;<b>4 RCCMS disposed · MR 2/2026-27 pending</b></div></div></div>
   <div class="col"><h2>Development controls</h2><div class="kv">
     <div>Permitted use / source &nbsp;<b>Agricultural · RMP 2015 (PD 30)</b></div>
     <div>FAR / coverage &nbsp;<b>Farm house ≤ 250 m² plinth</b></div>
     <div>Setbacks / plot &nbsp;<b>Plot ≤ 1.2 ha per farm house</b></div>
     <div>Height limit / basis &nbsp;<b>G+1 · ESZ rules apply</b></div></div></div>
  </div>
  <h2 style="margin-top:5.5mm;border:0;padding:0;margin-bottom:3mm">Edge conditions</h2>
  <table class="t">
   <tr><th style="width:21mm">Edges</th><th>Adjoining condition</th><th style="width:46mm">Clearance / width</th><th style="width:34mm">Evidence</th></tr>
   <tr><td>A–G · W (330 m)</td><td>Bannerughatta village: 1–2 storey houses, a waste and debris yard near D–E; lake beyond</td><td>Houses adjoin; lake {{fmt(lake1.dist_m)}} m W; park {{fmt(pa.dist_m)}} m W</td><td>Esri 2026 · Overture</td></tr>
   <tr><td>G–J · S (157 m)</td><td>Scrub and earth tracks; village lanes and houses to the south</td><td>No frontage road; housing 42 m S</td><td>Esri 2026 · Overture</td></tr>
   <tr><td>J–M · E (211 m)</td><td>Earth track; industrial sheds, then Bannerghatta Road (SH-87)</td><td>Industrial {{fmt(sens.industrial_nearest_m)}} m SSE; 45 m plan road {{fmt(proad.dist_m)}} m ESE</td><td>Overture · RMP 2031 layer</td></tr>
   <tr><td>M–A · NE (136 m)</td><td>Houses and a track; Ryan International School north</td><td>School {{fmt(sens.school_nearest.dist_m)}} m N; quarry {{fmt(sens.quarry_nearest_m)}} m N</td><td>Overture land use</td></tr>
  </table>
  <div class="impl"><div class="glbl">Design / development implication</div>
  <p>Two rules, not an edge, control: Agricultural zoning (non-farm use needs DC conversion) and the park's eco-sensitive zone. Get the BDA zonal certificate and the ESZ overlay for Sy 21–22, and reconcile the KML with the survey sketch, since the Sy 21 point falls 63 m outside it.</p></div>
 </div>
</section>

<!-- 04 TOPOGRAPHY -->
<section class="page">{{ head('TOPOGRAPHY','Terrain & the ground beneath',4) }}
 <div class="body">
  <img class="fig" src="{{fig.terrain}}" style="height:96mm">
  <div class="cap"><b>SOURCE</b> &nbsp;/&nbsp; Copernicus GLO-30 DSM (30 m, resampled to 10 m), {{ter.contour_interval_m}} m contours, over Esri imagery. A–B follows the fitted fall line.</div>
  <div class="row" style="margin-top:7.5mm;gap:0">
   <div style="width:72mm"><div class="lbl">Elevation range</div><div class="big">{{'%.0f'|format(ter.elev_min)}} / {{'%.0f'|format(ter.elev_max)}} m</div><div class="small">EGM2008 · DSM includes canopy</div></div>
   <div style="width:56mm"><div class="lbl">Typical slope</div><div class="big">{{'%.1f'|format(ter.plane_slope_pct)}} %</div><div class="small">Moderate · falls to the {{ter.fall_dir}}</div></div>
   <div class="col"><div class="lbl">Contour interval</div><div class="big">{{ter.contour_interval_m}} m</div><div class="small">GLO-30 DSM / 30 m</div></div>
  </div>
  <h2 style="margin-top:7.5mm">Transect A–B</h2>
  <img src="{{fig.transect}}" style="width:100%;height:29mm;object-fit:contain">
  <div class="cap"><b>SOURCE</b> &nbsp;/&nbsp; Section A–B sampled every 5 m from the DSM; A is south-east, B north-west.</div>
  <div class="small" style="margin-top:3.5mm;font-size:8pt">Section length {{fmt(tr.length_m)}} m &nbsp; / &nbsp; Relief {{'%.1f'|format(tr.relief_m)}} m &nbsp; / &nbsp; Vertical exaggeration ≈ {{'%.0f'|format(ve)}}×</div>
  <div class="impl"><div class="glbl">Design / development implication</div>
  <p>About {{'%.0f'|format(ter.relief_m)}} m of fall across the parcel, {{'%.1f'|format(ter.plane_slope_pct)}}% to the {{ter.fall_dir}}; only {{'%.0f'|format(ter.share_lt5_pct)}}% of the ground is under 5%. Terrace buildings along the contours, with the low NW corner ({{'%.0f'|format(ter.low_pt_z)}} m) kept for drainage. Expect retaining of 1–2 m per terrace; confirm with a ground survey.</p></div>
 </div>
</section>

<!-- 05 SUN -->
<section class="page">{{ head('SUN & SOLAR EXPOSURE','Light, shade & orientation',5) }}
 <div class="body" style="top:52mm">
  <div class="row" style="gap:6.5mm">
   <div style="width:110mm"><div class="glbl" style="margin-bottom:3.5mm">01 &nbsp;/&nbsp; Sun path</div><img class="fig" src="{{fig.sunpath}}" style="height:87mm"></div>
   <div class="col"><div class="lbl" style="margin-bottom:3.5mm">Seasonal comparison</div><img src="{{fig.sunpolar}}" style="width:100%;height:57mm;object-fit:contain">
     <div class="small" style="margin-top:3mm">21 Mar · 21 Jun · 21 Dec; {{sol.tz}}<br>True north; noon altitude {{'%.0f'|format(sol.events['21 Dec'].noon_alt)}}° (Dec) to {{'%.0f'|format(sol.events['21 Jun'].noon_alt)}}° (Jun, sun to the north)<br>Day length {{'%.1f'|format(sol.events['21 Dec'].daylength_h)}}–{{'%.1f'|format(sol.events['21 Jun'].daylength_h)}} h; no context model</div></div>
  </div>
  <div class="cap"><b>SOURCE</b> &nbsp;/&nbsp; Solar positions computed (NREL SPA, pvlib) for the site centroid; stereographic dome, Esri imagery. Hour lines at the 21st of each month.</div>
  <div style="border-top:.6pt solid #ddd;margin-top:5.5mm;padding-top:5mm"><div class="glbl" style="margin-bottom:3.5mm">02 &nbsp;/&nbsp; Solar radiation</div>
  <div class="row" style="gap:7mm">
   <div style="width:92mm"><img src="{{fig.solar}}" style="width:100%;height:65mm;object-fit:contain"></div>
   <div class="col"><div class="lbl">Analysis period</div><div class="mid">{{sol.years[0]}}–{{sol.years[1]}} monthly means</div>
     <div class="lbl" style="margin-top:6mm">Incident solar energy</div><div class="big" style="font-size:23pt">{{fmt(sol.ghi_year_kwh)}} kWh/m²</div>
     <div class="small">Horizontal plane, per year ({{'%.2f'|format(sol.ghi_day_mean)}} kWh/m²·day)<br>Highest wall exposure: SE / SW ≈ {{fmt(sol.faces_kwh.SE)}}; north {{fmt(sol.faces_kwh.N)}}<br>Best month {{MON[sol.best_month-1]}}; cloud cuts {{sol.cloud_loss_pct|int}}% vs clear sky</div></div>
  </div>
  <div class="cap"><b>SOURCE</b> &nbsp;/&nbsp; NASA POWER CERES SYN1deg monthly GHI {{sol.years[0]}}–{{sol.years[1]}}; wall split modelled from clear-sky geometry scaled to it.</div></div>
  <div class="impl"><div class="glbl">Design / development implication</div>
  <p>The site falls to the NW, so its slope faces the cooler afternoon side. Lay terraces E–W where possible, with main rooms facing N and S: the noon sun stays above {{'%.0f'|format(sol.events['21 Dec'].noon_alt)}}°, so short overhangs shade both. West walls take ≈ {{fmt(sol.faces_kwh.W)}} kWh/m²·yr: shade them with the existing tree clusters.</p></div>
 </div>
</section>

<!-- 06 WIND -->
<section class="page">{{ head('WIND & MICROCLIMATE','Air movement & outdoor comfort',6) }}
 <div class="body">
  <div class="row" style="gap:6.5mm">
   <img class="fig" src="{{fig.windmap}}" style="width:121mm;height:81mm">
   <div class="col"><img src="{{fig.windrose}}" style="width:100%;height:50mm;object-fit:contain">
    <div class="lbl" style="margin-top:4mm">Season / height</div><div class="mid" style="font-size:11.5pt">2015–24 / 10 m</div>
    <div class="small">Annual: from {{wst.annual.prevailing}}, mean {{wst.annual.mean_speed}} m/s, calm {{wst.annual.calm_pct}}%<br>Jun–Sep: {{sm.prevailing}} {{sm.prevailing_pct|int}}%, {{sm.mean_speed}} m/s<br>Dec–Feb: {{wi.prevailing}} {{wi.prevailing_pct|int}}%, {{wi.mean_speed}} m/s</div></div>
  </div>
  <div class="cap"><b>SOURCE</b> &nbsp;/&nbsp; NOAA ISD hourly observations, {{wst.name}}, {{wst.dist_km}} km NNE; consistent with NASA POWER MERRA-2 (from {{wmd.annual.prevailing}}, {{wmd.annual.mean_speed}} m/s).</div>
  <div class="row" style="margin-top:7mm">
   <div class="col"><h2>Local comfort</h2><img class="fig" src="{{fig.comfort}}" style="height:62mm"></div>
   <div class="col"><h2>Seasonal temperature</h2><img src="{{fig.temperature}}" style="width:100%;height:62mm;object-fit:contain"></div>
  </div>
  <div class="row"><div class="col cap"><b>SOURCE</b> &nbsp;/&nbsp; ESA WorldCover 2021 (10 m) on Esri imagery; dashed = 500 m ring.</div>
  <div class="col cap"><b>SOURCE</b> &nbsp;/&nbsp; NASA POWER MERRA-2 daily, {{cli.years[0]}}–{{cli.years[1]}}. HAL station mean {{wst.t_mean}} °C; hottest day {{wst.t_hottest[1]}} °C ({{wst.t_hottest[0]}}).</div></div>
  <div class="impl"><div class="glbl">Design / development implication</div>
  <p>The monsoon westerly ({{sm.mean_speed}} m/s) arrives over the village and park edge; open the built form to the W and let it run down the NW slope. Winter easterlies come off SH-87 and the industrial sheds, so plant a dust and noise screen on the E edge. April is the hot month (mean max {{cli.tmax_peak[0]}} °C).</p></div>
 </div>
</section>

<!-- 07 RAIN -->
<section class="page">{{ head('RAINFALL & WATER','Runoff, storage & groundwater',7) }}
 <div class="body" style="top:52mm">
  <div class="row" style="gap:6.5mm">
   <div style="width:110mm"><div class="glbl" style="margin-bottom:3.5mm">Surface response</div><img class="fig" src="{{fig.runoff}}" style="height:79mm"></div>
   <div class="col"><div class="lbl" style="margin-bottom:2mm">Monthly rainfall</div><img src="{{fig.rainfall}}" style="width:100%;height:31mm;object-fit:contain">
     <div class="lbl" style="margin-top:7mm">Event basis</div><div class="big" style="font-size:20pt">{{q10|int}} mm / 24 h</div>
     <div class="small">10-year return period (Gumbel on {{cli.amax_1day_years[0]}}–{{cli.amax_1day_years[1]}} annual maxima)<br>Mean annual {{fmt(cli.rain_annual_mean)}} mm; {{cli.rain_jun_nov_pct|int}}% falls May–Nov</div></div>
  </div>
  <div class="cap"><b>SOURCE</b> &nbsp;/&nbsp; D8 flow on GLO-30 DSM; Overture water. Rain: NASA POWER MERRA-2 grid {{cli.grid[0]}} N {{cli.grid[1]}} E (shared with north Bengaluru).</div>
  <h2 style="margin-top:6mm">Groundwater &amp; recharge</h2>
  <img src="{{fig.groundwater}}" style="width:100%;height:27mm;object-fit:contain">
  <div class="cap"><b>SOURCE</b> &nbsp;/&nbsp; Conceptual section on A–B. Strata and water depths from the CGWB Bengaluru Urban profile, not site boreholes.</div>
  <div class="row" style="margin-top:6mm">
   <div class="col"><div style="font-size:12pt;font-weight:700;margin-bottom:2.5mm">Surface water</div><p class="grey" style="font-size:8.6pt">Low point NW corner ({{'%.0f'|format(ter.low_pt_z)}} m) → village drain → lake {{fmt(lake1.dist_m)}} m W (0.8 ha).<br>10-yr day on {{fmt(geo.area_ha,2)}} ha: ≈ {{fmt(vol_now,-2)}} m³ runoff now (C 0.35), ≈ {{fmt(vol_built,-2)}} m³ built (C 0.75).<br>Basis: catchment = site; no city drain data this far south.</p></div>
   <div class="col"><div style="font-size:12pt;font-weight:700;margin-bottom:2.5mm">Ground conditions</div><p class="grey" style="font-size:8.6pt">District water level 5–30 m bgl pre-monsoon (CGWB).<br>Anekal extraction 106% of recharge (2025-26): over-exploited.<br>Granite-gneiss, weathered 10–30 m; check for rock outcrops.</p></div>
  </div>
  <div class="impl"><div class="glbl">Design / development implication</div>
  <p>Slope speeds runoff to the village on the NW: hold ≈ {{fmt(vol_built - vol_now,-2)}} m³ in terrace swales and a detention pond at the NW corner before discharge. Groundwater is over-drawn: plan on rainwater harvesting and reuse, not new borewells.</p></div>
 </div>
</section>

<!-- 08 LANDSCAPE -->
<section class="page">{{ head('LANDSCAPE & ECOLOGY','Living systems & views',8) }}
 <div class="body">
  <img class="fig" src="{{fig.landscape}}" style="height:92mm">
  <div class="cap"><b>SOURCE</b> &nbsp;/&nbsp; Esri imagery; park boundary and water from Overture Maps (OSM-derived); plan-view sight lines from the site centre.</div>
  <div class="row" style="margin-top:7mm;gap:13mm">
   <div class="col"><h2>Landscape structure</h2>
    <div style="display:flex;gap:3mm;margin:3mm 0 1mm"><img src="{{ic_land}}" style="width:29%"><img src="{{ic_veg}}" style="width:29%"><img src="{{ic_built}}" style="width:29%"></div>
    <div style="display:flex;gap:3mm" class="small"><div style="width:32%">Landform</div><div style="width:32%">Vegetation</div><div style="width:32%">Built form</div></div>
    <div class="kv" style="margin-top:5mm">
     <div>Canopy cover &nbsp;<b>{{'%.0f'|format(lc.canopy_site)}}% site · {{'%.0f'|format(lc.canopy_ring)}}% 500 m ring</b></div>
     <div>Permeable ground &nbsp;<b>{{'%.0f'|format(lc.permeable_site)}}% site · {{'%.0f'|format(lc.permeable_ring)}}% ring</b></div>
     <div>Water / habitat edge &nbsp;<b>park {{fmt(pa.dist_m)}} m · lake {{fmt(lake1.dist_m)}} m</b></div>
     <div>Tree survey / season &nbsp;<b>none · WorldCover 2021</b></div></div></div>
   <div class="col"><h2>View &amp; habitat priorities</h2>
    <div class="txt" style="font-size:9pt;line-height:1.45">Retain<br><b style="font-weight:400">The tree clusters on the slope and a green link west toward the park ({{'%.0f'|format(pa.area_km2)}} km² mapped).</b><br><br>Investigate<br><b style="font-weight:400">Elephant and leopard movement at the park edge, and quarry blasting and dust ({{sens.quarries_1km}} quarries within 1 km, nearest {{fmt(sens.quarry_nearest_m)}} m).</b></div>
    <div class="small" style="margin-top:9mm">Observer: site centre, plan view (no eye-height model)<br>Park boundary as mapped in OSM; ESZ limits not mapped here</div></div>
  </div>
  <div class="impl"><div class="glbl">Design / development implication</div>
  <p>Treat the west half as the landscape buffer facing the park: low, dispersed buildings, native planting, dark-sky lighting and wildlife-safe fencing. Keep built form toward the east, where the industrial edge already is.</p></div>
 </div>
</section>

<!-- 09 CONTEXT -->
<section class="page">{{ head('BUILT CONTEXT & ACCESS','Neighbourhood fit & movement',9) }}
 <div class="body" style="top:52mm">
  <img class="fig" src="{{fig.context}}" style="height:71mm">
  <div class="cap"><b>SOURCE</b> &nbsp;/&nbsp; Overture Maps buildings and roads (release 2026-09-23) over Esri imagery; A–B is a 1.2 km W–E section through the site.</div>
  <div class="glbl" style="margin-top:6mm">Street &amp; skyline profile A–B</div>
  <img src="{{fig.skyline}}" style="width:100%;height:21mm;object-fit:contain;margin-top:2mm">
  <div class="cap" style="margin-top:1mm">{{sky.n}} buildings cut; none carry mapped heights, so hatched blocks use storeys assumed from footprint (2–4 floors × 3.2 m).</div>
  <div style="border-top:.6pt solid #ddd;margin-top:4mm;padding-top:4mm" class="row">
   <div style="width:76mm"><div class="glbl" style="margin-bottom:3mm">Daily access</div><img class="fig" src="{{fig.isochrones}}" style="height:70mm">
    <div class="cap">Walking 5 / 10 / 15 min at 4.8 km/h on the Overture road network from the nearest road nodes.</div></div>
   <div class="col"><div class="lbl">Access basis</div><div class="mid" style="font-size:12pt">SH-87 side / walk / weekday</div>
    <div class="kv" style="margin-top:4mm">
     <div>Transit &nbsp;<b>{{inf.bus_stop.name}} stop · {{fmt(inf.bus_stop.dist_m)}} m</b></div>
     <div>Bus stand &nbsp;<b>Bannerghatta BMTC · {{'%.1f'|format(inf.bus_station.dist_m/1000)}} km</b></div>
     <div>Metro &nbsp;<b>Kalena Agrahara (Pink Line) ≈ 6 km</b></div>
     <div>Health &nbsp;<b>{{poi.Health[1].name}} · {{poi.Health[1].walk_min|int}} min</b></div>
     <div>Education &nbsp;<b>{{poi.Education[0].name.split(',')[0]}} · {{poi.Education[0].walk_min|int}} min</b></div>
     <div>Banking &nbsp;<b>{{poi['Daily needs'][0].name}} · {{poi['Daily needs'][0].walk_min|int}} min</b></div></div>
    <div class="txt" style="margin-top:5mm;font-weight:700;font-size:9.2pt;line-height:1.4">No public road touches the boundary; access is by earth tracks to SH-87 ({{fmt(R.context.major_roads.primary.dist_m)}} m E). Secure a frontage or easement first.<br>Context: village houses (median footprint {{R.context.bld_500_footprint_median|int}} m²) and industrial sheds; low-rise G+1 fits.</div>
    <div class="small" style="margin-top:4mm">Overture 2026-09-23.0 · checked {{DATE}}</div></div>
  </div>
 </div>
</section>

<!-- 10 PEOPLE -->
<section class="page">{{ head('PEOPLE, HISTORY & IDENTITY','The context beyond the boundary',10) }}
 <div class="body" style="top:52mm">
  <div class="row">
   <div class="col"><div class="glbl" style="margin-bottom:3.5mm">Land-use change</div><img class="fig" src="{{fig.landuse_change}}" style="height:45mm"><div class="cap"><b>SOURCE</b> &nbsp;/&nbsp; Esri Wayback releases 27 Feb 2017 (left) and 24 Sep 2026 (right).</div></div>
   <div class="col"><div class="glbl" style="margin-bottom:3.5mm">People &amp; activity</div><img class="fig" src="{{fig.density}}" style="height:45mm"><div class="cap"><b>SOURCE</b> &nbsp;/&nbsp; Built-footprint density from Overture buildings, 2026; activity proxy.</div></div>
  </div>
  <div class="row" style="margin-top:6mm">
   <div class="col"><div style="font-size:12.5pt;font-weight:700;margin-bottom:2.5mm">Recorded change</div><p class="grey" style="font-size:8.6pt">2017 → 2026: the parcel stays open scrub; the village grew to the W and sheds filled the E edge.<br>WorldCover 2021: {{'%.0f'|format(lc.site.Shrubland + lc.site.Grassland)}}% shrub and grass, {{'%.0f'|format(lc.site['Built-up'])}}% built.<br>Heritage: Champakadhama temple (Hoysala, 1257 CE) in Bannerghatta; quarries nearby.</p></div>
   <div class="col"><div style="font-size:12.5pt;font-weight:700;margin-bottom:2.5mm">Community needs</div><p class="grey" style="font-size:8.6pt">Bannerughatta GP: about 4,062 households (SECC); {{R.context.bld_500_n}} buildings within 500 m.<br>Daytime: zoo and park visitors, {{R.access.counts_1km.Education}} schools and colleges within 1 km.<br>Only {{R.access.counts_1km.Health}} health places within 1 km: a clinic or nature-education use fits.</p></div>
  </div>
  <h2 style="margin-top:6mm">Local architectural vocabulary</h2>
  <div class="row" style="gap:4.5mm">
   <div class="col"><img class="fig" src="{{ph_court}}" style="height:16mm;border-radius:1.2mm"><div style="font-weight:700;font-size:9.5pt;margin-top:3mm">Front yard</div><div class="small" style="font-size:6.8pt;margin-top:1mm">Tiled house, Puttur</div></div>
   <div class="col"><img class="fig" src="{{ph_ver}}" style="height:16mm;border-radius:1.2mm;object-position:50% 70%"><div style="font-weight:700;font-size:9.5pt;margin-top:3mm">Veranda</div><div class="small" style="font-size:6.8pt;margin-top:1mm">Pillared front, Melukote</div></div>
   <div class="col"><img class="fig" src="{{ph_roof}}" style="height:16mm;border-radius:1.2mm;object-position:50% 30%"><div style="font-weight:700;font-size:9.5pt;margin-top:3mm">Roof form</div><div class="small" style="font-size:6.8pt;margin-top:1mm">Clay-tile roofs, Krishnarajapet</div></div>
   <div class="col"><img class="fig" src="{{ph_street}}" style="height:16mm;border-radius:1.2mm;object-position:50% 60%"><div style="font-weight:700;font-size:9.5pt;margin-top:3mm">Street edge</div><div class="small" style="font-size:6.8pt;margin-top:1mm">Jagali steps, Malavalli</div></div>
  </div>
  <div style="font-size:14.5pt;font-weight:700;line-height:1.3;margin-top:6.5mm">Low, tiled roofs and raised verandas let rural Old Mysore houses sit lightly on sloping, rocky ground: a fit for a park-edge site.</div>
  <div class="small" style="margin-top:4mm;font-size:6.9pt">Wikimedia Commons, CC BY-SA 4.0: Prof tpms (Melukote, Krishnarajapet, Malavalli); Bharathesha Alasandemajalu (Puttur) &nbsp;/&nbsp; Old Mysore and coastal Karnataka examples, not on-site records</div>
  <div class="impl"><div class="glbl">Design / development implication</div>
  <p>Step low, pitched-roof pavilions with deep verandas down the slope, rather than one large footprint: it suits G+1 and the park edge.</p></div>
 </div>
</section>

